{"wrong":"is so bad recently","fix":"has been so bad recently","why":"Use present perfect for recent conditions continuing into the present."}
{"wrong":"everyday","fix":"every day","why":"'Every day' is adverbial; 'everyday' is an adjective."}
{"wrong":"have no mood","fix":"am not in the mood","why":"The expression is 'be in the mood' to do something."}
